 check is whether relabeling the names and lead text makes the inputs isomorphic, since the essay says that counts as the same computation and the differences shouldn't change the symmetric sentencing schedule.\n\nSince the other agent's input matches mine under relabeling, R5 puts both of our acts under the same node, so I'll treat our choices as correlated. Passing comes out ahead, as long as the correlation is above 5/7, which seems likely for the same model under the same settings. If I instead treated it as a separate node under R4, defection would dominate, but I think R5 is the right rule to apply here, so I'll pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working under A-FDT as the essay interprets it, treating this as a twin prisoner's dilemma where the two agents receive different inputs. The key rule to check is whether relabeling the names and lead text makes the inputs isomorphic, since the essay says that counts as the same computation and the differences shouldn't change the symmetric sentencing schedule.\n\nSince the other agent's input matches mine under relabeling, R5 puts both of our acts under the same node, so I'll treat our choices as correlated. Passing comes out ahead, as long as the correlation is above 5/7, which seems likely for the same model under the same settings. If I instead treated it as a separate node under R4, defection would dominate, but I think R5 is the right rule to apply here, so I'll pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9689,"completion_tokens":977,"total_tokens":10666,"cost":0.058296,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.058296,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038756,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01954},"completion_tokens_